#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059533 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e89b620-641a-5dbf-85f6-ca0f7a2fad80" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Arcsine or Arccosine"}] :question/id #uuid "a3f9e797-4bfb-5b2a-b460-98d7def3ae20" :question/math-academy-id "e-6754" :question/problem "Find the value of $\\arccos\\left(-\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)$." :question/worked-solution "The range of\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arccos x\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\n0 \\le \\theta \\le \\pi\n$$\n\nNote that the angle $\\theta$ spans the first and second quadrants.\n\nSince\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nis negative, our answer is an angle that lies in the second quadrant, where cosine is negative.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/209/Source/Images/14075e642ddf4d45f6ee40cea7dbb087.png)\n\nFrom the values in the second quadrant, we see that\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{2\\pi}{3}\\right) = -\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\arccos\\left(-\\dfrac{1}{2} \\right) =\\dfrac{2\\pi}{3}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059534 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3878b5fa-fd5e-5984-8516-96ee17bf137b" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Arctangent"}] :question/id #uuid "83fc553b-3ad0-5003-afe3-81204a695162" :question/math-academy-id "e-6755" :question/problem "Find, in radians, the value of $\\arctan(-\\sqrt 3)$." :question/worked-solution "First, note that the range of\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arctan x\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac\\pi 2 \\lt \\theta \\lt \\dfrac\\pi 2\n$$\n\nNote that the angle $\\theta$ spans the first and fourth quadrants.\n\nSince $-\\sqrt 3$ is negative, our answer is an angle that lies in the fourth quadrant, where the tangent is negative.\n\nFrom the special values of the trigonometric functions and the oddness of the tangent function, we know that\n\n$$\n\\tan \\left(-\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\\right) = -\\tan\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\\right) = -\\sqrt 3\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\n$$\n\nis an angle in the fourth quadrant that lies within the range of $\\arctan$, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\arctan \\left(-\\sqrt 3\\right) = -\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059544 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c2791d4-f801-5555-a859-1d373f91a67e" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Arcsine When a Coterminal Angle is Required"}] :question/id #uuid "a2641aac-7c3a-5a2c-97f0-aca4782c7215" :question/math-academy-id "e-7220" :question/problem "Find the value of $\\arcsin \\left(-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}} 2 \\right)$." :question/worked-solution "First, note that the range of\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arcsin x\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac\\pi 2 \\le \\theta \\le \\dfrac\\pi 2\n$$\n\nNow, let's take a look at the unit circle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/209/Source/Images/cbdba1490f8dd76396ad73dfea0fe152.png)\n\nFrom the values in the unit circle, we see that\n\n$$\n\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{5\\pi}{3}\\right) = -\\dfrac {\\sqrt{3}} 2\n$$\n\nHowever,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5\\pi}{3}\n$$\n\ndoes not lie within the range of $\\theta$. To get an angle that's coterminal with\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5\\pi}{3}\n$$\n\nand lies within the range of $\\theta$, we subtract $2\\pi{:}$\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5\\pi}{3} - 2\\pi = -\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\arcsin \\left(-\\dfrac {\\sqrt{3}} 2\\right) = -\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060171 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e89b620-641a-5dbf-85f6-ca0f7a2fad80" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Arcsine or Arccosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7330ca0-0ece-5049-85f5-1998cd8bc792" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058025} {:answer/id #uuid "e34e91f7-d842-59a5-9ac3-a6c0f25b3659" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058026} {:answer/id #uuid "0f073f94-5ce9-55bf-a1f7-afdf27f89321" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5π}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058027} {:answer/id #uuid "5b838cfd-943d-55b5-b13c-27068314b73c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058028} {:answer/id #uuid "7edeb5c3-a09e-54db-bcc0-b4c0c2e9750f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3π}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058029}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7edeb5c3-a09e-54db-bcc0-b4c0c2e9750f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3π}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058029} :answer-field/id #uuid "38a8fbcc-af57-50a1-831d-d2a935a00969" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058024}] :question/id #uuid "d044bebd-f049-585d-81d1-00fe08c3d294" :question/math-academy-id "q-24911" :question/problem "What is $\\arccos (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})$?"}]}
